  chef: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 556ecd75ee852ce4a93c60357c4eb4f6, type: 2}
  letterBody: 'Ciao again!


    Giulia here. Your garlic pasta has fans, I hear.
    Brava! Now a true Roman classic.


    Carbonara has started more arguments in
    my family than politics. Cream or no cream? (No cream.) My nonna would leave
    the table if you asked.


    Take the pan off the heat before the egg goes in.
    Toss fast, add pasta water, and let the hard cheese melt into a silky sauce.
    Too hot and you have scrambled eggs.


    Some rules are worth keeping. Most
    of them came from someone''s nonna.'
